[2026.09.07-23.27.40:689][ 70]LogVoxelWeather: the sky clock is not running (voxel.Sky.Enabled 0 or TimeScale 0), so the wind is frozen at epoch 0.000 s. With voxel.Sky.Enabled at 0 that epoch is 0, not wherever the clock had got to -- the sky clears its state when it is switched off. The wind is still spatially varying and still correct; it just will not change.
[2026.09.07-23.27.40:689][ 70]LogVoxelWeather: VoxelWeather bound to /Game/Voxel/MPC_VoxelSky.MPC_VoxelSky -- both wind parameters present. Driven every frame.
